# Family A32: SQS settlement batching (driverkit/flush). See
# hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./driverkit/flush
BENCH=BenchmarkSettleFlush
REF=immediate
AUTO_KEY=flush
ADR=13
TITLE="SQS settlement batching (A32)"
# The policies live in the root module rather than in drivers/sqs because the
# decision is broker-independent -- every broker whose settlement is a priced
# round trip faces the same four answers -- and because hack/bakeoff.sh runs
# one `go test` in PKG from the repository root: a root-module `go test` cannot
# reach a nested driver module's package (assumption A24.7, and family A29's
# own failure). The SQS driver binds a kind through Kind.Batching and the
# mechanism stays driverkit.BatchSettler's.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="cost, ack latency, shutdown correctness -> hybrid (<= 100 ms flush) expected"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: driverkit/flush has no
# IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX branch, and its arms are three arrival rates plus the pure
# decision.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="rate=1 rate=10 rate=100"
# roundtrips/settlement is "cost" -- the API calls the service charges for --
# latency/settlement is "ack latency" in the reference simulation's virtual
# microseconds, and held is "shutdown correctness" as a number: what a Close
# had to drain. ns/op is what the policy's own code costs and is NOT the
# criterion: `Submitted` is two integer comparisons in every kind, so a
# microbenchmark of the decision returns the same number four times.
DECIDED_ON="roundtrips/settlement latency/settlement held ns/op"
# The arrival rate is settlements per ticker interval, and it is the only
# dimension that separates the four kinds: at one per interval every kind but
# immediate makes one call per settlement, and at a hundred the two
# count-bearing kinds make one per ten.
